419:html[data-theme="light"] [class*="bg-white/[0.0"] {
424:   `text-white`/`bg-white`/`border-white` (bare, 100% opacity) are headings and
426:   slash after "white" is an OPACITY variant — `white/10`, `white/[0.04]`,
427:   `hover:bg-white/20` — and those want a wash relative to whatever the
430:   sm:, etc.) precedes the utility. Gradient stop utilities (from-white/N,
431:   via-white/N, to-white/N) are not covered — those set a custom property
441:html[data-theme="light"] [class*="bg-white/"]:not(.nx-dark-island, .nx-dark-island *) {
444:html[data-theme="light"] [class*="border-white/"]:not(.nx-dark-island, .nx-dark-island *) {
447:html[data-theme="light"] [class*="text-white/"]:not(.nx-dark-island, .nx-dark-island *) {
